From e72eb138baa9e4ceb855f871074bdbda450e6b21 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "HT9045 Machine (V906)" <Claude_RDBC_02@honprec.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 22:27:05 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] HTDESIGNER-97: Shift+drag draws a marquee from anywhere, like
 Blend (0.97.0)

Blend (Artboard modifier keys): "Select by drawing a marquee: hold down Shift
and drag". Here a marquee only started on the empty background, so a page
crowded with panels was hard to box-select. Now a Shift press on a component
starts a pending marquee (shiftEl): dragged 4 px it is the usual marquee
(what it encloses is selected); let go without a drag it is the Shift+click
as before (added / taken out). WPF_DIFF_LOG.md: item 26 done; Blend's
"Shift+click the first and last = adjacent objects" recorded as not changed
(adjacent = the Objects panel's order; the component tree already does that
range, the surface keeps XAML Designer's Shift+click = multi-select).

Tests (all 4 layers pass: lib 160, smoke 186, panels, real VS Code 159):
probe (started on box A, the marquee encloses only box B -> B; a Shift+click
on A then -> A and B; both pages).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
